{
  "_comment": [
    "Down where people walk, `high`'s antonym. `low clouds` brings the cloud deck down to a few",
    "blocks over the sea, so on most land you stand inside it -- the low-clouds step, written on purpose -- and",
    "`low landmass` takes the height out of the land. A low Age does both, and now and then has a low sea or short",
    "grass too.",
    "",
    "`low sea` stands the water down, `low sky` hangs the clouds in it, `low structures` are sunk partway into the",
    "ground, `low gravity` pulls lightly, `low grass` stays short and `low obelisks` (spikes, pyramids, arches,",
    "pedestals, piles) stand half as tall; `low lakes` lie down by the sea and a `low aurora` along the horizon. A low sun or moon keeps to the horizon."
  ],
